==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
If you have [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], it will be a great help for rushing down the enemy base before the enemies became threats. Otherwise, use Area Attackers such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Paris Cat]], or [[Crazed Bahamut Cat]], alongside with meatshields and [[Rover Cat Mk II]], if you have it. Alternatively, wait for the first Doge Dark to reach the base and use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat) |Can Can Cat]] or other high damaging attackers, then wait until you get enough money and send [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat) |Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

==='''Chapter 2 (Cheese)'''===
Simply use [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)]], Can Can Cat 32+, Awakened Bahamut Cat and this stage becomes trivial

'''Note''': Can Can MUST be level 32 to one shot the Doge Darks, otherwise this cheese won't work. If your Can Can has [[Money Up]], then Crazy Hearts combo is not even required, simply use a [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed wall]] to tank a hit from the Doge Dark and spawn Can Can.

At the beginning of the battle, use a Crazed Wall cat to tank a hit from the Doge Dark, then, use Can Can to swiftly kill the Doge Dark, once the Doge dark dies, save for Awakened Bahamut and deploy him as soon as you can. The rest of the level can be won by simply spaming meatshields and can can, Awakened Bahamut should kill the Hyppohs,Shibaliens and the base before the Heavenly Hippoes even spawn

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage still poses no threat, as it is almost identical to the past version. You can use high damage attackers such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to instantly kill the doge dark, and if you have their double-bounty talent, you can save money for [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat) |Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and rush the stage. If their double bounty is not available, you can use a starting-money UP combo and defend your units with meat shields such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall/Manic Eraser]] or [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono CC/Frolicking Nono]] is available.

